# Build-context allow list.
#
# Addition, not subtraction: exclude everything, then bring back only what the
# Dockerfiles COPY. A deny list silently leaks every directory the repo grows
# later — generated key material lives next to the code in this tree
# (config/, and keystores users create), and a build context that carries it
# hands it to the docker daemon even if no COPY line bakes it in.

# ── Layer 1: exclude everything, then bring back ─────────────────────
*
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

!sdk/proto/
# Standalone core conformance test input; never include the whole config/state tree.
!spec/vectors/token/tokens.vec
!robot/
!libpail_gate/
!examples/tb3/probe.go
!cloud/
!docker/entrypoints/
!docker/pail_split_entrypoint.sh

# Not scripts/ wholesale — key generators live there. _keymode.sh is the one
# file the gate image COPYs (the run-time copy of the key-mode predicate).
!scripts/_keymode.sh

# Not config/ wholesale — keys, certs and keystores live there.
!config/policy.yaml
!config/site_model.example.yaml
!config/sros2_policy.xml

# ── Layer 2: re-exclude INSIDE the allowed paths ─────────────────────
# Mostly redundant with the file-level allows above, kept because it also
# covers mistakes like a keystore placed under robot/ — the two layers stop
# different mistakes.
**/keys/
**/grpc_certs/
**/sros2_keystore/
**/*.pem
**/*_ed25519*.json

# Build artifacts and caches; install/ has been seen to hold keystore copies.
**/build/
**/install/
**/log/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
